INT. HIGH SCHOOL GYM - LOCKER ROOM - NIGHT

Cinderblock walls painted maroon. Benches bolted to the floor. A whiteboard with X's and O's smeared into gray.

COACH BARNABY "BARN" WHITLOCK, fifties, a whistle around his neck and a clipboard under his arm, paces. DRE, seventeen, the point guard. KENZIE, sixteen, a power forward, ties her sneakers. SAL, eighteen, a center, towel over his head. MOOKIE, fifteen, the smallest, bounces a ball. ILYA, seventeen, a transfer, stares at his hands.

COACH WHITLOCK
(to the room)
Listen up. Fourth quarter, eight points down. This is the league final. Eight points, four minutes.

DRE
We can do eight.

KENZIE
We've done more.

SAL
(muffled under the towel)
We have not.

COACH WHITLOCK
Sal, towel off your head.

SAL
Yes, Coach.

COACH WHITLOCK
Mookie, put the ball down.

MOOKIE
Sorry, Coach.

He doesn't put it down. Whitlock glares. Mookie tucks it under his arm.

COACH WHITLOCK
Dre, you bring it up fast. Kenzie, set the screen. Sal, roll to the rim. Ilya.

ILYA
Yes, Coach?

COACH WHITLOCK
You're the corner shooter.

ILYA
I missed my last four.

COACH WHITLOCK
You'll hit the next one.

ILYA
(to himself)
I don't know.

KENZIE
(to Ilya)
You will. Don't think.

COACH WHITLOCK
That's right. Don't think. Shoot.

A pounding at the door. A buzzer blares in the gym beyond.

COACH WHITLOCK
That's two minutes! Up!

The team rises as one. Dre slaps Sal's shoulder. Kenzie punches Ilya's arm, gently. Mookie scrambles onto a bench and, for a moment, stands taller than anyone.

MOOKIE
We got this!

COACH WHITLOCK
(drily)
Get off the bench, Mookie.

Mookie hops down. They form a circle, hands in the middle.

DRE
One, two, three.

ALL
Go!

They file out. Whitlock watches them go, then glances at the whiteboard and wipes it clean with his sleeve.

COACH WHITLOCK (CONT'D)
(muttering)
Eight points. Four minutes. Please.
